      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified composition retains an overall refractory character.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partially replacing Mo with Nb lowers the alloy's overall electronegativity difference.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A lower electronegativity difference produces fewer dislocation obstacles and a more balanced disordered BCC microstructure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo contributes to high yield strength but also increases lattice distortion and chemical-bonding differences associated with poor plasticity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-induced lattice distortion and bonding differences hinder slip.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb promotes ductility in similar refractory high-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing part of the Mo with Nb facilitates dislocation motion and plastic deformation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will have a higher room-temperature compressive plastic strain than equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will retain a room-temperature compressive yield strength near 1719 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed benefit requires the modified alloy to remain BCC and avoid secondary-phase formation.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Too little Mo replacement may provide insufficient ductility improvement, whereas too much may reduce strength.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
